# Per-repo exception to the LANGUAGE checks [2][3][4][5] of check-conventions.sh (docs/16 s6).
# Check [1], forbidden unicode, is language-neutral (docs/16 s4.2) and is NOT waived by this file.
#
# What docs/ko/ is: this repository's Korean-language control documents. They are the project's own
# original writing, NOT a reproduced external corpus, and the Korean and English sides are peer to
# peer with neither authoritative over the other (UPDATES.md section 2.2, and the CLAUDE.md
# copyright boundary). An earlier version of this file claimed the opposite; it had been copied from
# a different repository and contradicted the boundary this whole corpus is built on.
#
# Why the exception is needed, for exactly one check: docs/16 section 4.3 requires a Korean-language
# document to use natural Korean IT vocabulary, and these documents do, so the transliteration check
# [2] fires on them by design rather than by defect. The checker already exempts Korean-language
# documents from [2], but it keys that exemption on the file NAME, the "*.ko.md" suffix. This corpus
# is laid out as docs/<lang>/<theme>/<no>.md, so its Korean documents never match that suffix. This
# exclusion stands in for the exemption the layout cannot express.
#
# Measured against the live corpus, docs/ko/ produces hits on [2] only; [3], [4] and [5] are clean.
#
# docs/en/ is deliberately NOT listed. It produced zero hits on every check, so excluding it waived
# nothing and only widened the carve-out.
#
# The upstream fix is a path-based exemption for docs/ko/** in the playbook's own [2] skip list, next
# to the existing "*.ko.md" case. Once the playbook carries that, this file can be deleted. That
# matters for the migration: playbook v0.2.0 fails any conventions-exclude covering 40 percent or
# more of the tree, and docs/ko/ alone is about 47 percent here.
docs/ko/
